{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5404495","formula":"C₁₉H₂₅NO₂","hill":"C19H25NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":25.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"(±)-ethylketazocine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ethylketazocine (WIN-35,197-2), is an opioid drug of the benzomorphan family which has been used extensively in scientific research in the last few decades as a tool to aid in the study of the κ-opioid receptor. However, due to its relatively poor selectivity for the κ-opioid receptor over the μ- and δ-opioid receptors (of which it has approximately 80% and 20% of the affinity for, respectively, in comparison), as well as its relatively poor intrinsic activity at all sites (i.e., acts as a partial agonist with mixed agonist and antagonist properties), it has been mostly replaced in recent times by newer and more potent and selective compounds like U-50,488 and ICI-199,441."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":644273,"mass":299.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC[C@]12CCN([C@H](C1C)C(=O)C3=C2C=C(C=C3)O)CC4CC4","inchikey":"SEJUQQOPVAUETF-MKFRLIFGSA-N","iupac":"(1S,9R)-10-(cyclopropylmethyl)-1-ethyl-4-hydroxy-13-methyl-10-azatricyclo[7.3.1.02,7]trideca-2(7),3,5-trien-8-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"644273","atoms":47,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.942,"y":2.241,"z":-0.941,"el":"O"},{"x":5.049,"y":0.962,"z":0.628,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.855,"y":-0.261,"z":0.787,"el":"N"},{"x":0.75,"y":-1.44,"z":0.086,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.434,"y":-1.343,"z":-0.917,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.276,"y":-0.107,"z":-0.559,"el":"C"},{"x":0.14,"y":-1.563,"z":1.511,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.819,"y":0.993,"z":0.008,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.867,"y":-0.456,"z":1.851,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.821,"y":0.776,"z":1.133,"el":"C"},{"x":1.599,"y":-0.163,"z":0.021,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.676,"y":-0.149,"z":-0.394,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.262,"y":